{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "18", "m": "08", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "04", "M": "23", "S": "17"}}, "news": [{"title": "Guesthouse rooms, shops and guard cabins razed as DLF-3 drive resumes in Gurugram", "para": "On Monday, authorities in Gurugram took decisive action by sealing a guesthouse and dismantling illegal structures. This enforcement activity saw the removal of four unauthorized rooms in stilt parking areas and the clearing of commercial buildings along Moulsari Avenue Road and in V Block. Additionally, officials dismantled guard rooms occupying public land in front of residences, signaling ongoing efforts against illegal constructions in residential neighborhoods.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/guesthouse-rooms-shops-and-guard-cabins-razed-as-dlf-3-drive-resumes-in-gurugram/133311202?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-278192/133311202.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}, {"title": "Delhi government's housing colonies to get highrise makeover", "para": "The Delhi government is set to embark on an ambitious redevelopment project for PWD housing colonies. Under the TOD policy, existing flats will be transformed into sleek multi-storeyed buildings, with Gulabi Bagh, Kalyanwas, and Bahapur leading the initiative. This self-financing model will generate revenue from the sale of residential and commercial spaces to fund the new Delhi Secretariat complex construction.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/delhi-governments-housing-colonies-to-get-highrise-makeover/133311148?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-336224/133311148.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}, {"title": "MTNL, BSNL and RINL's \u20b913,500 crore worth of realty assets to hit markets", "para": "Realty assets worth an estimated \u20b913,500 crore belonging to MTNL, BSNL and RINL are set to hit the market after the Department of Public Enterprises gave final approval for their monetisation. The National Land Monetisation Corp will market 23 prime properties across six cities, targeting \u20b97,500 crore this fiscal.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/mtnl-bsnl-and-rinls-13500-crore-worth-of-realty-assets-to-hit-markets/133310892?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-137382/133310892.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}]}